WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.404 --> 00:00:04.354
Unit twenty-one. Clinical Research and Trials!

2
00:00:05.306 --> 00:00:10.285
Hello, everyone! I'm Doctor Sokha, your school doctor.

3
00:00:10.335 --> 00:00:13.774
Hi, Doctor Sokha! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.824 --> 00:00:18.993
Today we learn about Clinical Research and Trials. Let's go!

5
00:00:20.097 --> 00:00:24.731
Clinical trial. Say it with me. Clinical trial!

6
00:00:28.267 --> 00:00:33.317
Informed consent. Say it with me. Informed consent!

7
00:00:36.787 --> 00:00:40.604
Placebo. Say it with me. Placebo!

8
00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:48.344
Randomised. Say it with me. Randomised!

9
00:00:51.784 --> 00:00:56.184
Ethics committee. Say it with me. Ethics committee!

10
00:00:59.682 --> 00:01:03.615
Phases. Say it with me. Phases!

11
00:01:07.149 --> 00:01:10.932
Safety. Say it with me. Safety!

12
00:01:14.421 --> 00:01:18.338
Evidence. Say it with me. Evidence!

13
00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:34.676
A clinical trial tests treatments safely in phases. Randomised trials may use a placebo. Informed consent and an ethics committee protect participants and ensure reliable evidence.

14
00:01:34.726 --> 00:01:38.050
Now I understand. Thank you, Doctor Sokha!

15
00:01:38.739 --> 00:01:44.100
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:45.300
Placebo!

17
00:01:46.381 --> 00:01:51.787
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:51.837 --> 00:01:52.987
Safety!

19
00:01:54.085 --> 00:02:00.612
Did you know? Randomised controlled trials are considered one of the strongest types of evidence for treatments!

20
00:02:00.662 --> 00:02:02.719
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:04.089 --> 00:02:12.980
Think and answer. Why is informed consent essential in research?

22
00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:14.213
Great answer!

23
00:02:15.291 --> 00:02:20.715
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
